-- When a clause is checked against a type whose head is an implicit Π, here {u : ⊤} → bool
-- (after unfolding P), the checker inserts an implicit lambda. Its variable must not capture
-- the clause variable u (which used to happen when it was named after the binder of the type).

P ∷ U → U
P X = {u : ⊤} → X

f ∷ (u : bool) → P bool
f u = u
